{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on C2 (208a0378): the replica gives the fold and the\njudges the earlier entries. It comes from the state seed note,\ndraft 1, in review at b4d060ba (request c6eafabb), section 9.\n\nThe fact. The fold and the judges read earlier entries of the\nscope's own journal through `Own`\n(`packages/derive/src/fields.ts`). `equal` reads\n`j.own?.(seq)?.hash ?? null` (`packages/derive/src/operand.ts`).\nWith no entry, a local fact reference keeps its long form and\nequals nothing, and no fault shows. `applyEntry` passes no `own`\nto the capacity bindings when its caller passes none\n(`packages/derive/src/fold.ts`), and a `floor` entry throws\nwithout one. So a replica that passes no `Own` can judge an act\ndifferently from the scope, with no sign.\n\nThe ruling, for C2:\n1. The replica keeps each entry that it folds, while the scope\n   holds that entry.\n2. The replica gives `applyEntry` and `judgeAct` an `Own` over\n   those entries. It builds `Own` as the scope does.\n3. The replica never answers \"no entry\" for a position that the\n   scope holds and the replica lacks.\n4. A scope with a floor still stops the client with `archived`\n   in C2. The start from a seed is slice SS2 of the note.\n\nBefore the code of C2, send me one act:\n- each read of `Own` and of `fixedHash` in `packages/derive`,\n  with what the reader does when the entry is absent,\n- how the replica builds `Own`, and whether `ownOf` of\n  `packages/scope` can move to a place that both use.\n\nIn C2, measure the memory of a replica at 20,000 entries, in Node\nand in headless Chrome. If a page cannot hold that, propose a\nsmaller form that keeps item 3.\n\nThe generated test of C2 gains one case: `judgeAct` on the\nreplica equals `judgeAct` on the scope's state for an act that\ncompares a fact of the scope's own journal.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}